Generated by `Submission/Work/RTOwed/scratch/emit_wall_data.py` from the validated cusp development
`rtdata/data/uhs_cusp_data.json` (see `scratch/wall_table.py` for the exact check: for all 288
walls the relation below holds exactly, on rational sample points of the wall).

For the cube `a`, coordinate `i` and side (`0` = the lower face `{y i = cubeCorner a i}`,
`1` = the upper face `{y i = cubeCorner a i + 1}`):

* `wallNb a i side` is the cube of the *far* side of the wall (the cube into which the reduction
  sends the points just across the wall),
* `wallLam a i side` is the lattice vector `lambda` with `far = near - lambda`,
* `wallGam a i side` is the element of `Gg = (Fin 4 -> ZMod 2) x ZMod 2` of the identification: the
  sign change of the Klein coordinates and the copy bit.

The certificate (delegated as `Work.RTOwed.chartKlein_wall`) is

  `chartKlein (wallNb a i side) (y - wallLam a i side, s) = act (wallGam a i side).1 (chartKlein a (y, s))`

for `y` on the wall and `y` in the cube `a`.

Do not edit by hand.
-/
